---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<p style="text-align: center;">check out <a href="https://www.instagram.com/jbronen/">my instagram</a> to find upcoming shows 🙂</p>
			<h2>About</h2>
			<img src="/headshot-optimized.jpg" alt="Jared Bronen Headshot" style="width: 150px; float: right; margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);" />
			<p>Hello, and welcome to my website.</p>
			<p>
				I'm a Brooklyn-based writer, filmmaker, and comedian. I wrote and directed the short film
				The Debut with my writing partner Alex Guaglianone, which was selected as a finalist at
				<a href="https://comedypro.hahaha.com/public/detail/shows/the-debut--404/#:~:text=TITLE%3A%20The%20Debut%20LOGLINE%3A%20A,course%20of%20their%20lives%20forever">Just for Laughs</a>
				Montreal in 2025 in partnership with Electric Avenue. My debut short Pick a Random Number (linked below)
				played at several film festivals in 2023 / 2024.
			</p>
			<p>
				Currently, I co-host a monthly show at the Upright Citizens Brigade in NYC called The Trash King,
				which is a tournament of bits celebrating comedy that is both dumb and high commitment. It has been
				featured in the <a href="https://nycomedyfestival.com/lineup/the-trash-king/">New York Comedy Festival</a>
				and written up in <a href="https://www.jezebel.com/trash-king-comedy-show-fart-jokes-are-back">Jezebel</a>
				and <a href="https://www.timeout.com/newyork/comedy/the-trash-king">Timeout NY</a>. We've taken the show
				to UCBLA, Fun and Dumb Festival in Brooklyn, and iO Fest in Chicago.
			</p>
			<p>
				I wrote for UCBNY's Maude Night (the house sketch team program) for several years, writing and acting
				for Ponyboy both at UCB and SF Sketch Fest. Before that, I wrote for Like Butter at the PIT, Cherry, Cherry
				for Boogiemanja, and several other indie sketch teams. I also wrote for CollegeHumor 2012-2013, and had a
				recurring role in the Jake & Amir web-series as <a href="https://jakeandamir.fandom.com/wiki/Mike_Fink_(Character)">Mike Fink</a>.
			</p>
			<p>
			    I currently teach Sketch at Brooklyn Comedy Collective and work as a software engineer at Google, 
				where I develop C++ and Java applications.
			</p>

			<h2>Shorts</h2>
			<h3><a href="https://filmfreeway.com/projects/3544341">The Debut</a></h3>
			<p>
			(Comedy) - A woman organizes a cabin getaway for her friends to debut a new comedy character that will change the course of their lives forever.<br>
				<ul>
					<li><a href="https://comedypro.hahaha.com/public/detail/shows/the-debut--404/#:~:text=TITLE%3A%20The%20Debut%20LOGLINE%3A%20A,course%20of%20their%20lives%20forever">Just for Laughs Shorts</a>, Finalist - Montreal, QC 2025</li>
					<li><a href="https://www.lesfilmfestival.com/films-2026/the-debut">Lower East Side Film Festival</a>, Official Selection - New York, NY 2026</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
			
			<h3><a href="https://filmfreeway.com/projects/2697090">Pick a Random Number</a></h3>
			<p>
			(DocuFiction / Comedy) - A scientist explains how computers measure naturally occurring phenomena to "pick" random numbers. Then, he searches for the ultimate source of randomness.
				<iframe class="pagelayer-video-iframe" width="100%" height="400" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Plx-cJik2n8?autoplay=0&mute=0&loop=0&playlist=Plx-cJik2n8" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe>
				<ul>
					<li><a href="https://www.tootsiesvideovault.com/">Tootsie's Video Vault</a> - New York, NY June 2024<br>
						Award: Best Film, Hidden Gems</li>
					<li><a href="https://www.rawsciencefilmfestival.com/2023-films">Raw Science Film Festival</a> - Los Angeles, CA October 2023<br>
						Award: Best Dramatic Short</li>
					<li><a href="https://shitinthedirt.com/">Shit in the Dirt Film Festival</a> - Portland, ME June 2023<br>
						Award: Most Coherent Film</li>
					<li><a href="https://www.chainfilmfestival.com/">Chain Film Festival</a> - New York, NY 2023<br>
						Official Selection</li>
				</ul>
			</p>

			<h2>Writing</h2>
			<p>PDFs available on request</p>
			<p>
				Shrek’s in the City: (Comedy) a parody of fish-out-of-water comedy pilots featuring Shrek, who, for reasons unknown to him, has taken the form of a human man living in modern-day New York City. Things go a little haywire as he learns to adjust to our crazy way of life!
			</p>
			<p>
				Content Moderator: (Horror / Sci-Fi) feature screenplay about a contract moderator working for a large social media company who starts seeing personally disturbing imagery in his review queue.
			</p>
